  "notes": "{責|せ}める means to blame, criticize, or torment someone.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を particle: {彼|かれ}を{責|せ}める\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {自分|じぶん}を{責|せ}める: to blame oneself\n- {責|せ}めないで: don't blame (me/them)\n- {責|せ}められる: to be blamed (passive)\n\nNUANCES:\n1. Blame/criticize: Finding fault with someone\n2. Torment: Causing mental or physical distress\n\nHOMOPHONE DISTINCTION:\n- {責|せ}める: to blame, torment (責 = responsibility)\n- {攻|せ}める: to attack (攻 = attack) - military/sports context\n\nRELATED:\n- {責任|せきにん}: responsibility\n- {非難|ひなん}する: to criticize (more formal)",
